<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Nagorno-Karabakh War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1988">1988</a>–<a href="/years/1994">1994</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as First Karabakh War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagorno-karabakh">Nagorno-Karabakh</a> War was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and Armenian forces over Nagorno-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karabakh">Karabakh</a>, an Armenian-majority region of Soviet Azerbaijan, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> collapsed. Armenian forces took the region and seven surrounding districts, and hundreds of thousands of people on both sides were displaced. A Russian-brokered ceasefire in May 1994 froze the conflict until the war of 2020.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-nagorno-karabakh-war.jpg" alt="First Nagorno-Karabakh War" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicholas Babaian, Oleg Litvin, Jalpeyrie, MarshallBagramyan, collage: Gulustan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karabakhwar01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
